    "type": "question",
    "label": "60",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of $x^4$ from the expansion of $$\\frac{(1+x)^8}{x}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\binom{8}{5}=56$",
      "worked": "After division by $x$, the general term is\n$$\\begin{align*}T_k&=\\binom{8}{k}x^{k-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $x^4$ term,\n$$\\begin{align*}k-1&=4\\\\k&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe coefficient is $\\binom{8}{5}=56$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
